  "description": "HAXPAB crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C48 H103 Co3 Dy3 N3 O28 2+,2(N1 O3 1-),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Co13 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co14 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co16 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy9 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy11 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Co17 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co21 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co23 (Co) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.280-3.937 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 98.78-111.27°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [(CoIII)3Dy3(μ3-OH)4(O2CtBu)6(teaH)3]·(NO3)2·H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
